WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Good morning, teacher and classmates.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.500
My name is Mai Như Ý, class 11A9, and this is my partner.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.800
My name is Nguyễn Thành Đạt, in class 11A9.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.500
Today, we are excited to present a vision

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.800
of the ideal living space for humanity in the coming decades.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.800
That's right. Welcome to our Green City of the Future model,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.200
where modern technology doesn't clash with nature,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.300
but blends with it to protect the environment and improve our lives.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.500
Let's explore how this amazing city works.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:34.200
Beneath the surface, underground water flows

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.500
to run a mini hydropower station and a geothermal plant

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.000
that taps into the Earth's natural heat.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.200
This keeps the city self-sufficient with zero harmful emissions.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.500
Beyond clean electricity, the transport system is 100% eco-friendly.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:58.000
High above the streets, an elevated train provides fast transit and prevents traffic jams.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.500
Down on the ground, residents use electric cars and bicycles, keeping the air fresh and quiet.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.800
And above all, we also feature a flying car for future aerial transit.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.500
What makes the skyscrapers here special is their safety and sustainability.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:21.500
Inside the central tower, a giant tuned mass damper

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.000
absorbs shock and keeps the building stable during strong winds or earthquakes.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.000
On the roof, an early disaster warning radar station

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.200
detects extreme weather early to keep residents safe.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.500
Surrounding the buildings are green roofs and large parks

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:45.500
that act as the city's natural lungs.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:51.500
Through this model, we want to share a simple message:

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:58.000
a smart city isn't just about tall buildings, it's about respecting nature and sustainable science.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.500
The future isn't far away. It starts with how we protect the environment today.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:08.000
Thank you, teacher and everyone, for listening to our presentation!
